        {
          "title": "Observability and Debugging: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Structured Logging",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One JSON object per line==: `level`, `time`, `msg` plus fields",
                "Machine-searchable, not free-text strings"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{\"level\":30,\"time\":1730000000000,\"msg\":\"login ok\",\"userId\":42}"
              ],
              "note": "filter by userId, level or time"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Tools and Where Logs Go",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:Logs}",
                  "What happened in **prod**"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Inspector}",
                  "Step through **live** code"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:Heap snapshots}",
                  "Why memory **grows**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Log to ==stdout only==",
                "Docker, systemd, k8s collect and ship the logs",
                "App never manages files or rotation"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. console.log vs pino",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "console.log",
                "pino"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Format",
                  "unstructured text",
                  "{green:JSON}"
                ],
                [
                  "Levels",
                  "none",
                  "{green:leveled}"
                ],
                [
                  "Context",
                  "no child loggers",
                  "child loggers"
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "synchronous-ish",
                  "fast"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistake",
              "text": "Never build logs with `'user ' + id`. Pass fields as an ==object==, `logger.info({ userId }, 'login')`, so they stay queryable."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pino and Log Levels",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pino and Log Levels",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Setup and Levels",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const logger = require('pino')({",
                "  level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'info'",
                "})",
                "logger.info({ userId }, 'login ok')"
              ],
              "note": "object first, message second"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "trace",
                "debug",
                "info",
                "warn",
                "error",
                "fatal"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "10",
                  "20",
                  "30",
                  "40",
                  "50",
                  "60"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A level logs ==itself and everything above it==",
                "`info` drops `debug` and `trace`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Errors and Secrets",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "logger.error({ err }, 'payment failed')",
                "",
                "pino({ redact: [",
                "  'req.headers.authorization', 'password'",
                "] })"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`err` serializer keeps {green:type}, {green:message}, {green:stack}",
                "A plain string {red:loses the stack}",
                "`redact` masks the listed paths in output",
                "Never log tokens, passwords or full card data"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Dev vs Production",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "pino-pretty is dev only",
              "text": "`node app.js | pino-pretty` in dev. In production, pipes and transports add cost and defeat ==raw JSON== shipping."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Request IDs and Child Loggers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Request IDs and Child Loggers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Request ID",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Request ID== = unique ID per request, on **every** log line",
                "Filter one request's logs across the whole flow",
                "Reuse incoming `x-request-id`, else `crypto.randomUUID()`",
                "{green:Echo} it back in the response header"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const id = req.headers['x-request-id']",
                "  || crypto.randomUUID();",
                "res.setHeader('x-request-id', id);",
                "req.log = logger.child({ reqId: id });"
              ],
              "note": "middleware: one child logger per request"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Child Logger and AsyncLocalStorage",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`logger.child({ reqId })` adds ==reqId== to every line it writes",
                "No repeated passing of fields",
                "Passing the logger through every function is **tedious**",
                "`AsyncLocalStorage` (`node:async_hooks`) holds the per-request logger",
                "Readable anywhere in the async call chain"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const { AsyncLocalStorage } = require('node:async_hooks');",
                "const als = new AsyncLocalStorage();",
                "als.run(req.log, next);  // in middleware",
                "const log = () => als.getStore();  // anywhere"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Across Services",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "x-request-id?",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Service A",
                    "sub": "reuse or generate",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Outbound call",
                    "sub": "x-request-id header",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Service B",
                    "sub": "same reqId in logs",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Broken trace",
              "text": "If a downstream service gets **no** `x-request-id`, it makes a new one and the trace is ==broken==. Forward the ID on every outbound call."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
